+- `npm test` runs the built-in Node test runner for visual preference persistence and synchronization.
+- `npm run check` runs ESLint, Prettier check, the test suite, TypeScript, and production build.
+
+## Visual Preferences
+
+The backdrop variant and color theme are stored together as a versioned JSON record under
+`localStorage` key `tahion.visual.preferences`:
+
+```json
+{ "version": 1, "variant": "signal", "theme": "acid" }
+```
+
+When the record is absent, valid values from the legacy raw-string keys
+`tahion.backdrop.variant` and `tahion.backdrop.theme` are migrated independently without
+removing or changing those keys. Missing data uses the `signal` and `acid` defaults without
+writing at startup. Valid changes in another open tab update the controls and backdrop through
+the browser `storage` event; invalid or unrelated events are ignored.
 
